{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1768 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "6dd642c74ca87a9c997b2b57f142b7615f26811cd4c9cbe9b82cf715743ffbfe" :edb/db-before-t 1767 :edb/db-after-t 1768 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535080 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:23:33.537Z" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166630 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\ln(x + y)$.\nUsing a substitution of the form $z= x + y$, transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z'(x) = f(z)$. What is the function $f(z)$?" 13194139535080 false] [17592186166630 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\ln(x + y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z= x + y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z'(x) = f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166630 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x + y\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dz}{dx} - 1 &= \\ln z\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form\n\n$$\nz'(x) = f(z)\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\ln z+1\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(z) = \\ln z + 1\n$$" 13194139535080 false] [17592186166630 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x + y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 1 + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = \\ln z+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = \\ln z + 1.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166631 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = x + y.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y) = x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166631 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = x + y$.\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n$g(x,y) = x+C$,\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)$?" 13194139535080 false] [17592186166631 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x+y\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 + \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dz}{dx} - 1 &= z\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form\n\n$$\nz'(x) = f(z)\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = z+1\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{z + 1}\\frac{dz}{dx} &= 1 \\\\\n∫\\frac{1}{z + 1}dz &= ∫dx \\\\\n\\ln \\mid z + 1 \\mid &= x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\ln{\\mid x+y+1 \\mid} = x + C\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x,y) = \\ln{\\mid x+y+1 \\mid}\n$$" 13194139535080 false] [17592186166631 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 1 + \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = z+1.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|z+1| & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\ln{|x+y+1|}  = x + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y) = \\ln{|x+y+1|}.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330130 13194139535080 true] [17592186166780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330137 13194139535080 true] [17592186166780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330144 13194139535080 true] [17592186166780 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330151 13194139535080 true] [17592186166781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330158 13194139535080 true] [17592186166781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330165 13194139535080 true] [17592186166781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330172 13194139535080 true] [17592186166781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330179 13194139535080 true] [17592186166993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535080 true] [17592186166993 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = e^{x + 2y + 5}$.\nUsing a substitution of the form $z = x + 2y$, transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z^{′}(x) = f(z)$. What is the function $f(z)$?" 13194139535080 false] [17592186166993 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+2y+5}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+2y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166993 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2} & ={e}^{z+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{z+5}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2{e}^{z+5}+1.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166994 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535080 true] [17592186166994 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{y+3x+2}-3.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186166994 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\sqrt{y + 3x + 2} - 3$.\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n$g(x, y) = x + C$,\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x, y)$?" 13194139535080 false] [17592186166994 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=y+3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3 & =\\sqrt{z+2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{z+2}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z+2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int (z+2)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2(z+2)^{1/2} & =x+C \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z+2} & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{y+3x+2} & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=2\\sqrt{y+3x+2}.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330130 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330131 13194139535080 true] [17592186330130 1089 "q-108800" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330130 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535080 true] [17592186330130 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={cos}^{2}⁡(2x-y+1).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=2x-y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330130 1113 #uuid "0cadc7d0-f55e-571e-8683-ef2ab01dbbf4" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330130 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=2x-y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={cos}^{2}⁡(z+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2-{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1).$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330132 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330133 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330134 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330135 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330136 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330134 13194139535080 true] [17592186330131 1110 #uuid "15f66041-f44e-5006-9cb0-51f8c7140a45" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330132 1034 "{cos}^{2}⁡(2z+1)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330132 1111 #uuid "02a0f214-a82f-5ad4-90a7-51deda39e430" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330133 1034 "1+{cos}^{2}⁡(2z)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330133 1111 #uuid "285cd11a-8f32-5914-8bd4-901e35ae2c5d" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330134 1034 "2-{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330134 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330134 1111 #uuid "0fb9646e-3136-5d4a-8060-63be7ea26403" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330135 1034 "2-{cos}^{2}⁡z" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330135 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330135 1111 #uuid "ef32ba9f-bd30-54e4-b321-0263fc7e08eb" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330136 1034 "2{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330136 1111 #uuid "38971647-8caf-5c5b-a7d8-2045d02ffa26" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330137 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330138 13194139535080 true] [17592186330137 1089 "q-108802" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330137 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535080 true] [17592186330137 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={tan}^{2}⁡(3x-5y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=3x-5y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330137 1113 #uuid "769fb03f-07ef-54c0-8e28-ab259b3c1d36" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330137 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=3x-5y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3-5\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={tan}^{2}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330139 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330140 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330141 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330142 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330143 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330140 13194139535080 true] [17592186330138 1110 #uuid "79e07e1d-12ba-5797-b106-4412c6ccd42a" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330139 1034 "1+{tan}^{2}⁡z" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330139 1111 #uuid "611d910a-f061-5d9b-8e02-dfab64887b98" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330140 1034 "3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330140 1111 #uuid "869ccc6c-69d1-5f0b-8761-4d264cf47322" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330141 1034 "3-{tan}^{2}⁡(z-5)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330141 1111 #uuid "c7030cb8-72e5-5adb-992a-af6fe5d08de5" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330142 1034 "5-3{tan}^{2}⁡z" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330142 1111 #uuid "1c9cd66f-e4bb-5662-abb7-6ace6be09272" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330143 1034 "3+5\\operatorname{tan}⁡z" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330143 1111 #uuid "8d336402-c00c-53ea-a816-7ea4fd82377b" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330144 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330145 13194139535080 true] [17592186330144 1089 "q-108806" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330144 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535080 true] [17592186330144 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(5y-7x+2)^{5}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=5y-7x,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330144 1113 #uuid "53bd63e0-b7c8-588a-b02f-e455261c85c3" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330144 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=5y-7x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-7\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{7}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{7}{5} & =(z+2)^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5(z+2)^{5}-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=5(z+2)^{5}-7.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330146 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330147 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330148 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330149 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330150 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330146 13194139535080 true] [17592186330145 1110 #uuid "ff2f6a15-42e3-5a01-a856-cd34e3fe1fab" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330146 1034 "5(z+2)^{5}-7" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330146 1111 #uuid "6e660202-5d83-572f-8d4c-d92fee11baa6" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330147 1034 "5(z+2)^{5}+1" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330147 1111 #uuid "a04aa864-9f87-5b4a-82db-5615de9b9bee" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330148 1034 "(z+2)^{5}-7" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330148 1111 #uuid "d7ea971f-84b0-52ee-a061-52b676f3e201" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330149 1034 "(z-2)^{5}+1" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330149 1111 #uuid "e1a72c85-fa92-5882-90ad-4f9e7ac46d1c" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330150 1034 "(z+5)^{2}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330150 1111 #uuid "937f797c-f9e6-5347-b97e-1082ac3b700a" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330151 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330152 13194139535080 true] [17592186330151 1089 "q-108821" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330151 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535080 true] [17592186330151 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{(x+y)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330151 1113 #uuid "a8b5df87-edf7-5da6-a482-ae2863c92ba3" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330151 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}+1.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330153 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330154 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330155 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330156 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330157 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330154 13194139535080 true] [17592186330152 1110 #uuid "2880ddbf-996b-5b4d-b960-2ba3c5b73276" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330153 1034 "1-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330153 1111 #uuid "bcc3e64b-ca52-54b7-bfdb-e1992800a84f" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330154 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}+1" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330154 1111 #uuid "cdfbcec4-811a-5a3b-bc07-00be21eb9ddf" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330155 1034 "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{e}^{2}}+1" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330155 1111 #uuid "eb9c8884-3f5d-52f0-9cf4-7bea005112a8" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330156 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{z}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330156 1111 #uuid "1faa357a-6ac2-53aa-a0b8-96edb9191b3c" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330157 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}-1" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330157 1111 #uuid "38ba1b00-7ff6-5edf-84ac-157cd5f4c444" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330158 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330159 13194139535080 true] [17592186330158 1089 "q-108855" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330158 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535080 true] [17592186330158 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{(x-2y)^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330158 1113 #uuid "ec7f57b2-2ef2-56bc-99a6-43d73009fa00" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330158 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x-2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1-2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{z}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{z} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}} & \\,⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{z}+\\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{z}-\\frac{1}{z} & =x+C \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1}{z} & =x+K \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1}{z} & =C-x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1}{x-2y}=C-x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1}{x-2y}.$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330160 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330161 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330162 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330163 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330164 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330161 13194139535080 true] [17592186330159 1110 #uuid "704ada25-3bfc-54cd-8f9e-e98a1a38a966" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330160 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330160 1111 #uuid "048b5deb-13d0-5721-b07f-ff26355736dc" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330161 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1}{x-2y}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330161 1111 #uuid "edaea162-9751-5441-93a6-f8eab2a98b57" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330162 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330162 1111 #uuid "4cd07fa4-645f-5ad9-8d88-af788fbf21df" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330163 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)-2}{x-2y}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330163 1111 #uuid "4bf8b0f2-1fe1-5f9e-856e-a506df1d9d52" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330164 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}{x-2y}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330164 1111 #uuid "447036c9-9619-5da1-af16-961df9abdaea" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330165 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330166 13194139535080 true] [17592186330165 1089 "q-108856" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330165 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535080 true] [17592186330165 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+y}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)}-1.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\frac{x}{2}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330165 1113 #uuid "4f2db63f-c6f6-53bb-b50f-fb394fae795a" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330165 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{z} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}} & \\,⟹\\,v=2\\sqrt{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-4\\sqrt{z} & =x+K \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-2) & =x+K \\\\ \\sqrt{z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-2) & =\\frac{x}{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{K}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2) & =\\frac{x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=\\sqrt{x+y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2).$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330167 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330168 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330169 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330170 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330171 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330168 13194139535080 true] [17592186330166 1110 #uuid "a0cc3624-9c91-5273-9673-260ede7d1559" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330167 1034 "\\sqrt{x+y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330167 1111 #uuid "c7ecfb8f-7928-5f4c-a51a-914dddb78405" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330168 1034 "\\sqrt{x+y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2)" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330168 1111 #uuid "6be975f6-ee24-57cc-8589-ed289767e760" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330169 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{x+y}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330169 1111 #uuid "028cc4a9-9ebd-5997-8a43-b5ec7985c28b" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330170 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+3" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330170 1111 #uuid "482e5744-893e-5031-b3c6-9b32ce3c882f" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330171 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2}{\\sqrt{x+y}}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330171 1111 #uuid "4f2812d5-d1c1-521b-8111-af3fb4a61791" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330172 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330173 13194139535080 true] [17592186330172 1089 "q-108858" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330172 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535080 true] [17592186330172 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{(2x+y)\\,{2}^{2x+y}}-2.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330172 1113 #uuid "86b98f38-121b-564d-b2ca-dbad04433775" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330172 1145 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=2x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2 & =\\frac{1}{z\\,{2}^{z}}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{z\\,{2}^{z}}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{2}^{z}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int z\\,{2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={2}^{z} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int z\\,{2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{z\\,{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{z\\,{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x+C \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(z-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x+K \\\\ {2}^{z}(z-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2x+y}(2x+y-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={2}^{2x+y}(2x+y-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}).$" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330174 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330175 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330176 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330177 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330178 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1041 "selection" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330176 13194139535080 true] [17592186330173 1110 #uuid "9d8050a1-bba8-57c7-a54e-0ea1deee6644" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330174 1034 "\\frac{{2}^{2x+y}}{2x+y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139535080 true] [17592186330174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535080 true] [17592186330174 1111 #uuid "cb5b46df-4b82-5e94-99bf-e0d7213f7907" 13194139535080